04-07  planted Dwarf Patio Peach in contained round bed by garage, surrounded by mints.
( Peach: dwarf ornamental form with double pink flowers; fruit is red/gold with small white-fleshed freestone. Leaves are long slender brilliant reddish purple throughout the season. Deciduous. Useful as accent or container plant. Hardiness zone 5-9. grown by Holland Nursery, Franklin, VA 23851.  Bought at Harris teeter, Chapel Hill, $29.99.)";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1519769042;s:8:"modified";i:1620515809;}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1620515809;s:2:"ip";s:14:"75.165.226.231";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:14:"garden:orchard";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:7:"[2021] ";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:19;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:3:"mcf";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";}}}